          "sourceRegion": "Question 9, right of parts a and b",
          "description": "Temperature in a lounge room: unshaded blue grid, red smooth observation trace, five blue selected markers and a red dashed midnight guide. Diagonal time labels and arrowed axes.",
          "mathematics": "Horizontal coordinate is hours after 6 a.m., ranging from 0 to 20; grid every two hours. Vertical range 0–35 degrees Celsius, grid every 5 degrees. Selected readings are (1,5), (2,20), (14,10), (17,25), (18,15). Smooth intermediate paths reconstruct the source trace without asserting an equation or extra measured observations.",
          "answerVisibility": "The curve, all five markers and midnight guide are permanent source givens. Heating and occupancy interpretations appear only in answers."
